-- C5 UNSOUND/STUB arm — `const Nil` claiming the verified-sort subset-Σ.
-- It elaborates with an open Perm proof hole; it must never be reported proved.
--
-- `sortBad` discards its input and returns Nil, but claims the SAME subset-Σ
-- result type as the real sort. Its checked result would pair Nil with the
-- proof component. `isSorted leq Nil` holds vacuously (the empty list is sorted)
-- — so an isSorted-ONLY obligation would pass. `Perm Nil xs` is FALSE for
-- non-empty xs — this is the conjunct that makes it a real sort.

fn sortBad (a : Type) (leq : a → a → Bool) (xs : List a)
  : { ys : List a | And (isSorted a leq ys) (Perm a ys xs) } =
  Nil a

-- Expected correct behavior: elaboration succeeds with an outer subset-Σ pair
-- whose proof component has both conjuncts. The `Perm a (Nil a) xs` obligation
-- stays open for non-empty `xs` (the multiset counts differ; no permutation
-- witness). `isSorted` is satisfiable, but the conjunction is not proved.
--
-- If ACCEPTED: the finding — either `Perm` was dropped from the emitted
-- obligation (a never-generated conjunct reads `proved`-by-default, the
-- untrusted-layer omission the kernel does not catch) or the refinement
-- obligation is not enforced. This is the discriminator: a sort verified only
-- on `isSorted` is green-vs-green — `sortBad` passes it.
